  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read in convert stream filters with NUL in line-break-chars\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-92842.patch: out-of-bounds read in convert stream filters with NUL in line-break-chars\n     - CVE-2026-92842\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: FastCGI allowed_clients compared only 96 bits of IPv6 addresses\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91768.patch: FastCGI allowed_clients compared only 96 bits of IPv6 addresses\n     - CVE-2026-91768\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read in php_openssl_matches_wildcard_name()\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91767.patch: out-of-bounds read in php_openssl_matches_wildcard_name()\n     - CVE-2026-91767\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: TLS peer name falls back to CN when the certificate has a service ID\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91769.patch: TLS peer name falls back to CN when the certificate has a service ID\n     - CVE-2026-91769\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: phar tar entry injection via unchecked entry size\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-6103.patch: phar tar entry injection via unchecked entry size\n     - CVE-2026-6103\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: unbounded recursion in SOAP XML parsing and decoding\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91765.patch: unbounded recursion in SOAP XML parsing and decoding\n     - CVE-2026-91765\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in SOAP HTTP chunked response handling\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-14181.patch: heap buffer overflow in SOAP HTTP chunked response handling\n     - CVE-2025-14181\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds read on empty Location header in HTTP redirects\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-93682.patch: out-of-bounds read on empty Location header in HTTP redirects\n     - CVE-2026-93682\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: credentials forwarded to another origin on HTTP redirects\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91766.patch: credentials forwarded to another origin on HTTP redirects\n     - CVE-2026-91766",
